# Known gaps: a backend that is missing a public name the other backends have.
#
# Format: <os> <seam> <name>
#
# Each line is a real parity gap that has NOT been fixed yet. Deleting a line is
# the proof it was fixed; the gate fails while a line is here but the backend
# declares that name, so this list can only shrink.
#
# linux: the Wayland backend has no headless render entry point, so the verify
# and inspect tooling cannot drive a frame there. Not app-breaking (the app uses
# the Driver, not Window.renderHeadless), but it is a capability the other three
# backends have.
linux window renderHeadless
